Aarrgh!  Ok, so I started playing Rogues recently.  I like that they
start with a pile of daggers and are deadly with them almost
immediately.  After about 20 false starts, I get a rogue that starts to
look survivable.  I cought a break in the mines by finding a +3
Dwarvish Mithril Coat.  The minetown altar was coaligned and a couple
of sacrifices brought me a +3 Stormbringer.  And I remembered not to
accidentally walk into the priest while it was equipped this time. ;)

No wishes at all until I found a double bones pile down at about level
14.  The bones also held a CoMR and one or two other goodies.  There
was one magic lamp in each bones and I happened to have plenty of holy
water.  The two wishes brought me +2 SDSM and +2 speed boots.

I got all the way down to the maze underneath Medusa due to a series of
pits and trapdoors.  I came back up a few levels and finished off
Medusa on the way.  I hadn't done the quest yet and I was at level 14
with around 120 hps.  I knew I had to fix this before going any deeper
or trying the quest.

I found Fort Ludios and cleaned it out.  It was surprisingly easy at
-14 AC and 120 Hps.  I never had any close calls.  60k zorkmids to a
priest on level 15 or so and my naked AC was at -1.  With partially
enchanted gear, and a full ascension kit thanks to another wish from a
smoky (gain energy), my AC was at a nice -29.  I hadn't found any magic
markers yet, so the only enchant armor scrolls I had were found, and
mostly used on foo proofing my armor.

I spent about 20 minutes mixing up full heal potions.  I had a ton of
potions from my explorations and managed to make 31 full heal potions.
This brought my hps up to a very survivable 380.

Ok, now for the quest!  I went in unspoiled and blundered my way down
to the last level with the Master Assassin.  I couldn't find a secret
door, and so I finally gave in and looked it up.  The prevailing
opinion was to poly into a Xorn or something.  So I took off my armor,
polymorphed, and walked into a room full of nagas and the master
assassin.

Now, I've killed plenty of nagas but I usually find them when I'm in
full armor, so I didn't know they could stun.  My hps dropped from 380
down to 130 or so before I recovered from the stun.  Panicked, I
quaffed a full healing potion, got stunned again, and back down to 150
hps.  Now, I had all kinds of options at this point.. My most obvious
solution was a teleport scroll.  Instead, I did the stupid thing and
tried to kill one of the monsters.  Stunned again, and the Master
Assassin had his way with me.

There's something heartbreaking about having a very ascendable
character die so stupidly.  Although, I definitely learned a thing or
two about the Rogue quest. 

